# Benefits and Health Insurance Policy
**Daisy Health**
**Policy ID:** HR-BI-002
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2025
**Last Reviewed:** June 1, 2025
**Owner:** People Operations

---

## Purpose

Daisy Health is committed to supporting the health and financial wellbeing of our employees and their families. This policy outlines the benefits available to eligible employees, including health insurance, dental, vision, mental health support, and tax-advantaged savings accounts.

---

## Scope

This policy applies to all full-time employees working 30 or more hours per week. Part-time employees working 20–29 hours per week are eligible for limited benefits as noted in each section. Contractors and temporary staff are not eligible for benefits under this policy.

---

## 1. Eligibility and Enrollment

### New Hire Enrollment

New full-time employees may enroll in benefits within **30 days of their hire date**. Coverage begins on the **first day of the month following the hire date**.

Example: If you are hired on March 10, your coverage begins April 1.

If you miss the 30-day enrollment window, you must wait until the next **Open Enrollment period** unless you experience a qualifying life event.

### Open Enrollment

Open Enrollment occurs annually each **November** for coverage beginning January 1 of the following year. Employees will receive notification via email at least 3 weeks before Open Enrollment opens.

### Qualifying Life Events

Outside of Open Enrollment, you may update your benefits within **30 days** of a qualifying life event, including:

- Marriage or domestic partnership
- Birth or adoption of a child
- Divorce or legal separation
- Loss of coverage from another plan
- Death of a dependent

---

## 2. Health Insurance

Daisy Health offers three medical plan tiers through our carrier network:

### Plan Options

| Plan | Monthly Premium (Employee Only) | Deductible | Out-of-Pocket Max |
|---|---|---|---|
| Daisy Bronze | $0 employee contribution | $2,500 | $7,000 |
| Daisy Silver | $85/month | $1,000 | $4,500 |
| Daisy Gold | $210/month | $250 | $2,500 |

Daisy Health covers **100% of the Bronze plan premium** for employees. Employees choosing Silver or Gold pay the difference shown above.

### Dependent Coverage

Employees may add dependents to their plan. Dependent premium contributions vary by plan and number of dependents. Details are available in the Benefits Portal.

### Virtual Care

As a Daisy Health employee, you have **complimentary access to Daisy Health's own virtual primary care platform** at no cost, regardless of your health plan selection.

---

## 3. Dental Insurance

Daisy Health offers dental coverage through our dental carrier:

- **Preventive care** (cleanings, x-rays): 100% covered, no deductible
- **Basic restorative** (fillings): 80% covered after $50 deductible
- **Major restorative** (crowns, root canals): 50% covered after deductible
- **Annual maximum benefit:** $2,000 per person
- **Orthodontia:** 50% covered up to $1,500 lifetime maximum

Employee monthly premium: $12/month. Dependent coverage available at additional cost.

---

## 4. Vision Insurance

- **Annual eye exam:** $10 copay
- **Frames or contacts:** $150 allowance per year
- **Additional frames discount:** 20% off beyond allowance

Employee monthly premium: $6/month.

---

## 5. Mental Health and Behavioral Health Benefits

Daisy Health takes mental health seriously. All employees have access to:

### Employee Assistance Program (EAP)

- **6 free therapy or counseling sessions per year** through our EAP provider
- Available to employees and household members
- Confidential — no information is shared with Daisy Health

### Behavioral Health Coverage

Mental health and substance use disorder services are covered at parity with medical benefits under all three health plans. This includes inpatient, outpatient, and telehealth mental health visits.

### Daisy Health Behavioral Health Team

Employees on Daisy Silver or Gold plans may access Daisy Health's own behavioral health counselors through the virtual care platform at no additional cost for up to 12 visits per year.

---

## 6. Health Savings Account (HSA)

Employees enrolled in the **Daisy Bronze plan** (a high-deductible health plan) are eligible for a **Health Savings Account (HSA)**.

- **Daisy Health contributes:** $500/year for employee-only coverage; $1,000/year for employee + dependents
- **2025 IRS contribution limits:** $4,150 (individual); $8,300 (family)
- HSA funds roll over year to year and are yours to keep even if you leave Daisy Health
- Funds can be used for qualified medical, dental, and vision expenses

Employees on Silver or Gold plans are not eligible for an HSA but may enroll in a **Flexible Spending Account (FSA)**.

---

## 7. Flexible Spending Account (FSA)

Employees on Daisy Silver or Gold plans may contribute to a Healthcare FSA:

- **2025 contribution limit:** $3,050
- Funds are available on day one of the plan year
- Use it or lose it — unused funds do not roll over (except up to $610 may roll over per IRS rules)
- Eligible expenses include copays, prescriptions, dental and vision costs

A **Dependent Care FSA** is also available for all employees, up to $5,000/year, for eligible childcare or elder care expenses.

---

## 8. Life and Disability Insurance

### Basic Life Insurance

Daisy Health provides **basic life insurance equal to 2x your annual salary**, up to $500,000, at no cost to you.

### Supplemental Life Insurance

Employees may purchase additional life insurance up to 5x their annual salary during Open Enrollment, subject to evidence of insurability for amounts over $250,000.

### Short-Term Disability (STD)

- Covers **60% of your base salary** for up to 12 weeks
- Begins after a 7-day waiting period
- Covers non-work-related illness, injury, or pregnancy recovery

### Long-Term Disability (LTD)

- Covers **60% of your base salary** after STD ends
- Maximum benefit period: to age 65
- Fully employer-paid

---

## 9. Retirement — 401(k) Plan

- Daisy Health offers a **401(k) plan** through our retirement provider
- Employees are eligible to contribute starting on their **first day of employment**
- **Daisy Health matches 100% of contributions up to 4% of your salary**
- Employer match vests on a **3-year graded schedule**: 33% after year 1, 66% after year 2, 100% after year 3
- 2025 IRS contribution limit: $23,500 (under age 50); $31,000 (age 50 and over)

---

## 10. Additional Benefits

- **Commuter Benefits:** Pre-tax transit and parking up to $315/month
- **Professional Development Stipend:** $1,000/year for courses, certifications, or conferences
- **Parental Leave:** 16 weeks fully paid for primary caregivers; 6 weeks for secondary caregivers (see Leave Policy HR-LV-006)
- **Fertility Benefits:** Up to $5,000 lifetime benefit for fertility treatments
- **Student Loan Assistance:** $100/month employer contribution toward student loan repayment

